  "steps": [
    "Soak 150g yellow moong dal for 1 hour. Drain it well.",
    "Take 100g of the soaked dal along with the green chillies and garlic. Add 2–3 tbsp water little by little and grind into a coarse, thick paste.",
    "Transfer the ground mixture to a bowl and whip it well for 1–2 minutes to incorporate air.",
    "Add the remaining 50g soaked whole dal, rice flour, coriander, cumin seeds, ajwain, red chilli powder, turmeric, and chaat masala. Mix everything well.",
    "Don’t add the salt, baking soda, or onion yet. Keep the batter thick.",
    "Preheat your air fryer to 200°C for 5 minutes.",
    "Once the air fryer is hot, add the chopped onion, salt, ¼ tsp baking soda, and 1 tsp hot oil to the batter. Mix well.",
    "Make small dollops of around 20–25g each.",
    "Lightly oil spray the dollops and air fry at 190°C for around 8 minutes.",
    "Flip them and spray with oil again a d air fry at 200°C for another 6–8 minutes, until deep golden and crispy. It’s completely okay if it sticks to the bottom, just scrape, flip and air fry. Mine stuck too but came out beautiful❤️",
    "For the dressing, mix 50g Skyr with 1 tbsp green chutney until smooth and creamy."
  ],
